[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue because its reports share subject lines
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and engineering closed it on 5 October.
Read by cause, it held three problems. Two are done. One is not.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 did not close the one-day moves. The parser fix reads dd/mm; it does not change
time zones. Reports of a booking one day off are still open, in their own ticket.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {repo} {rows} />

## How a report is placed

1. Count each report once, by `id`: the export repeats some rows across pages.
2. Its cause comes from its tenant (`causes.ts`), not from intake's tag, which is a guess from
   the reporter's browser: a booking-v3 tenant through the form is `hint`; any other day-first
   tenant is `parser`.
3. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) is also `shift`. The desk files
   it under its tenant's cause, so the counts above overlap by those reports.

## What is left

- `shift`: keep the booking's date in the tenant's time zone when invites are made and sent;
  check invites across zones and around clock changes. New reports of a booking one day off go to
  [#3](https://github.com/darco81/mega-dev-s01e03/issues/3), not to #4471.

## For the desk

Merging on subject alone put three problems into one ticket, and closing it hid the one nobody
fixed. Before marking a big ticket known, or closing it, group it by cause, not by subject.

